  "repo_truth": "Review 9 returned CHANGES_REQUIRED with zero Critical, six Required, and one Nit findings. The complete 81-path pre-remediation subject is frozen at sha256:7535dca0e75cf5b71280ccb56bb1491b6f42a995d99d45bc6c7b42fa4e21312a. The defects are limited to documentation: stale implementation-authority language; twelve omitted GitNexus commands; a superseded MoveFileExW acceptance item; an ambiguous UNICODE_STRING buffer representation; loss of exact raw NTSTATUS through DeviceIoControl for FSCTL_GET_OBJECT_ID; an incompatible retained-directory NtCreateFile option set; and stale todo status wording. Production, selectors, staging, and commit remain frozen.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Edit only the seven existing HCM-2.3 atomic-authority surfaces: SPEC, runtime contract, control schema, control vectors, plan, todo, and the atomic authority proof. Leave all Rust, tests, top-level phase documents, other proof files, and prior dispatches byte-exact.",
    "Repair SPEC opening authority language so implementation authorization is historical and superseded by the current documentation-only publication repair; retain the explicit production freeze and authorization order.",
    "Add both with-tests and without-tests exact GitNexus impact commands for native_bound_tokens, native_path_tokens, native_metadata_subjects, observe_retained_regular_file, same_native_metadata, and validate_native_publication_observation. Preserve all sixteen existing CRITICAL impact stops.",
    "Mark Review 3 MoveFileExW and MOVEFILE_WRITE_THROUGH acceptance text historical and superseded; no path-only publication primitive may satisfy the current retained-parent protocol.",
